# R8 rules for :app (AGP merges every file in src/main/keepRules). R8 full mode is on (AGP default;
# gradle.properties must not set android.enableR8.fullMode=false).
#
# Library coverage, checked against the release mapping (M7):
# - Hilt / Dagger: generated keep rules ship with the KSP output; nothing needed here.
# - Room: room-runtime keeps RoomDatabase subclasses' no-arg constructors, so RxDatabase_Impl
#   (found by name) keeps its name.
# - smbj / sshj / BouncyCastle / commons-net: :core:netfs/consumer-rules.pro.
# - Jellyfin media3-ffmpeg-decoder: its consumer rules keep the JNI surface (native method names
#   via -keepclasseswithmembernames, and FfmpegAudioDecoder.growOutputBuffer, which the native
#   code calls back). Media3's exoplayer rules keep FfmpegAudioRenderer's reflective constructor,
#   and R8 currently rewrites DefaultRenderersFactory's Class.forName("…FfmpegAudioRenderer")
#   to the obfuscated name.

# FFmpeg renderer: DefaultRenderersFactory (EXTENSION_RENDERER_MODE_PREFER) loads it by name and
# swallows ClassNotFoundException, so if the forName rewrite ever stops applying, AC3/E-AC3/DTS/
# TrueHD audio would silently stop playing. Keep the class name and that constructor outright.
-keep class androidx.media3.decoder.ffmpeg.FfmpegAudioRenderer {
    <init>(android.os.Handler, androidx.media3.exoplayer.audio.AudioRendererEventListener, androidx.media3.exoplayer.audio.AudioSink);
}
# JNI symbols are resolved by name (Java_androidx_media3_decoder_ffmpeg_<Class>_<method>); the
# consumer rule already covers this, restated with includedescriptorclasses so parameter types
# of native methods keep their names too.
-keepclasseswithmembernames,includedescriptorclasses class androidx.media3.decoder.ffmpeg.** {
    native <methods>;
}
